-- mu-nonpositive: an occurrence to the left of an arrow.  The field of
-- mk holds P in the domain of a function type, which is not a strictly
-- positive occurrence, so the family is refused with the M2 word of
-- D-M1-2 (SG-M1 kills the mutation that admits it).

mu P : Type 0 with
| mk : (P -> P) -> P
